            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0818" n="723" xml:id="pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/570: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-26T23:00:00+09:00">February 26, 1936—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 26—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. 1. The Tokyo <hi rendition="#italic">Nichi Nichi</hi> in an extra tonight
                    states that Home Minister Goto has been appointed as temporary acting
                    Premier.</p>
                <p>2. The Embassy has learned from a reliable informant who talked with Count Makino
                    this evening that Makino was neither killed nor wounded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
